    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but if the scientific consensus was so clear that the vaccines were safe and effective, doesn't that kind of make the liberty argument secondary? like, shouldn't the 'correct' ethical choice be the one that saves the most lives? it feels like prioritizing personal autonomy over public safety is just a bad way to run a society.",
