      "content": "Many public health ethicists support utilitarian arguments, suggesting that maximizing overall well-being and saving lives is the primary duty of society. This perspective views mandates as a necessary, albeit restrictive, measure to achieve the greatest good for the greatest number. However, critics argue that even with a strong scientific consensus, overriding fundamental personal rights requires extremely high thresholds of justification, or risk creating a dangerous precedent for government overreach.",
